Theorem 1. Let X be a random variable defined over (\u2126,F,P). Suppose f : R \u2192 R is a measurable function
(with respect to \u03c3-fields BR and BR). Then f(X) is a random variable.
Proof. Let Y = f(X). To prove the theorem it is enough to show that Y\u22121(\u2212\u221e,y] \u2208 F for all y \u2208 R. Let
y \u2208 R be fixed. We have
